nside the breast tissue designating the previous biopsy cavity  The cavity itself is located 0 6cm from the closest surgical resection margin  The specimen is submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity designated by the clip   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the remaining tissue  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final medial anterior superior margin left breast   is a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm portion of unoriented breast tissue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a predominantly fibrous breast tissue  This specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Julia Turbiner M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Kristina Braaten M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  The focus of severely atypical ductal hyperplasia present in the main specimen is present   0 05cm from the  unoriented  margin  The features of the focus border on ductal carcinoma in situ  The focus was reviewed with Dr  Koerner who concurs with this interpretation  Addendum  1 by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL MEDIAL ANTERIO SUPERIOR MARGIN   EXCISIO , Not Done.
