Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 03 ACCESSIONED ON  17 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 09 26 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast cancer  positive margins  History of invasive carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  FOCAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  RESIDUAL CARCINOMA IS NOT IDENTIFIED  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 14 34                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm left simple mastectomy specimen with an irregular REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm overlying portion of tan white skin containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm unremarkable eccentrically located nipple  Along the lateral aspect  6 0cm from the nipple  is a well healed 3 5cm in length scar  There is a short suture designating the superior and a long suture designating the lateral aspect  The anterior aspect is inked blue  and the posterior black  Within the infero lateral aspect of the deep posterior margin  there is a REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm thin walled  smooth  disrupted cavity which communicates directly with the posterior deep margin  The lining is tan pink  smooth and glistening with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm defect containing sutures which communicates with the anterior soft tissue aspect  The borders of the cavity are smooth and unremarkable  There is an ill defined tan white lobulated rubbery  fibrotic area which abuts the disrupted cavity  extending superiorly and medially  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  This fibrotic area comes to 0 6cm from the deep and 0 7cm from the anterior soft tissue margin  The remaining parenchyma consists of tan yellow to pink lobulated unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  Along the periphery no lymph nodes are identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Cavity to posterior margin  B  Cavity to anterior margin in area of suture defect  C D  Representative sections of cavity wall with cavity to subjacent rubbery  fibrotic tissue and deep margin in cassette D  E F  Ill defined fibrotic rubbery area  Gross Description by  JENNIFER NASH Resident  LYNN CORNELL  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael J Yaremchuk  M D  PART   BREAST LEFT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , Not Done.
