ly 2 0cm medial to this first cavity lies the second cavity which measures REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  The second cavity is present in the inner quadrant and contains tan brown hemorrhagic material  This cavity lies 1 0cm from overlying inked margin and 5 0cm from posterior margin  The breast parenchyma surrounding this cavity shows foci of yellow discoloration  The intervening breast parenchyma between these two cavities contains grossly unremarkable tan yellow lobulated cut surface interspersed with scant fibrous tissue  The remaining breast parenchyma contains tan yellow lobulated cut surface  No additional discrete mass or lesion is noted  The upper outer quadrant tissue is palpated for lymph nodes and no lymph nodes are grossly appreciated  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  first cavity in outer quadrant to include closest posterior and anterior inked margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire second cavity in inner quadrant to include closest posterior inked margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  fibrous breast parenchyma between the two biopsy cavities   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  fibrous breast parenchyma  inner most quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper outer quadrant tissue that may represent lymph nodes  Final Diagnosis by Joshua Kish M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  report_end  , Not Done.
